    {
      "id": "6656360",
      "title": "Resolving Dynamic Data with the resolve Guard",
      "lectureOrder": 476,
      "videoOrder": 437,
      "sourceHash": "66bbeaf42e0f49aa2b0b92ebcc959278c9ef16f79db66b7d0a22e434d2d8fac9",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.45,
          "end": 6.21,
          "en": "-: In the last lecture, we learned how to pass static data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 6.21,
          "end": 9.24,
          "en": "Now let's say we have some dynamic data we have to fetch",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 9.24,
          "end": 12.42,
          "en": "before a route can be displayed or can be rendered.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 12.42,
          "end": 14.1,
          "en": "For example, here on the servers,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 14.1,
          "end": 17.1,
          "en": "let's say these servers already have been loaded.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 17.1,
          "end": 19.62,
          "en": "But once we click a server here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 19.62,
          "end": 22.95,
          "en": "and maybe I should log in to demonstrate this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 22.95,
          "end": 27.15,
          "en": "I want to load the individual server from some backend.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 27.15,
          "end": 28.56,
          "en": "So we are going to simulate",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 28.56,
          "end": 32.58,
          "en": "that this takes a couple of milliseconds or seconds.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 32.58,
          "end": 33.963,
          "en": "So how could this work?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 34.92,
          "end": 39.18,
          "en": "If we have such a use case, we need a resolver.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 39.18,
          "end": 40.56,
          "en": "There's always a service",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 40.56,
          "end": 43.74,
          "en": "just like CanActivate or CanDeactivate,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 43.74,
          "end": 46.92,
          "en": "which will allow us to run some code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 46.92,
          "end": 48.78,
          "en": "before a route is rendered.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 48.78,
          "end": 51.12,
          "en": "Now the difference to CanActivate is",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 51.12,
          "end": 52.856,
          "en": "that the resolver will not decide",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 52.856,
          "end": 55.65,
          "en": "whether this route should be rendered or not,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 55.65,
          "end": 58.02,
          "en": "whether the component should be loaded or not.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 58.02,
          "end": 62.04,
          "en": "The resolver will always render the component in the end,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 62.04,
          "end": 64.5,
          "en": "but it will do some preloading, you could say.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 64.5,
          "end": 66.03,
          "en": "It will fetch some data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 66.03,
          "end": 68.25,
          "en": "the component will then need later on.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 68.25,
          "end": 71.07,
          "en": "Of course, the alternative is to render the component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 71.07,
          "end": 73.23,
          "en": "or the target page instantly,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 73.23,
          "end": 77.22,
          "en": "and in the OnInit method of this page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 77.22,
          "end": 78.72,
          "en": "you could then fetch the data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 78.72,
          "end": 81.03,
          "en": "and display some spinner whilst you're doing so.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 81.03,
          "end": 82.41,
          "en": "So that is an alternative.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 82.41,
          "end": 83.52,
          "en": "But if you want to load it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 83.52,
          "end": 85.368,
          "en": "before actually displaying the route",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 85.368,
          "end": 88.28999999999999,
          "en": "this is how you would add such a resolver.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 88.28999999999999,
          "end": 91.32,
          "en": "So let's say for the single server here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 91.32,
          "end": 94.02000000000001,
          "en": "I will add it in the Server, File,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 94.02000000000001,
          "end": 97.2,
          "en": "my server-resolver.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 97.2,
          "end": 99.68299999999999,
          "en": "And again, this will be technically just be a service.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 99.68299999999999,
          "end": 102.15,
          "en": "So I'll export my class here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 102.15,
          "end": 105.42,
          "en": "which I'll name ServerResolver.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 105.42,
          "end": 110.22,
          "en": "And now this has to implement the resolve interface",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 110.22,
          "end": 113.7,
          "en": "provided by @angular/router.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 113.7,
          "end": 116.31,
          "en": "Resolve is a generic type and it should wrap",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 116.31,
          "end": 120.39,
          "en": "whichever item or data field you will get here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 120.39,
          "end": 122.46,
          "en": "will fetch here in the end.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 122.46,
          "end": 124.792,
          "en": "So we will fetch a server here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 124.792,
          "end": 127.65,
          "en": "and therefore we should define the type here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 127.65,
          "end": 129.09,
          "en": "Now, you could outsource this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 129.09,
          "end": 131.94,
          "en": "into an interface or a model in general.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 131.94,
          "end": 134.37,
          "en": "So we will know that a server will have an id",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 134.37,
          "end": 136.68,
          "en": "which is of type number,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 136.68,
          "end": 139.32,
          "en": "that it will have a name which is a string,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 139.32,
          "end": 140.88,
          "en": "and a status, which is a string.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 140.88,
          "end": 144.15,
          "en": "So this is simply a type definition of,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 144.15,
          "end": 147.78,
          "en": "well, the thing this resolver will give us in the end",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 147.78,
          "end": 150.51,
          "en": "to what it will resolve in the end.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 150.51,
          "end": 153.464,
          "en": "Now the resolve interface requires us to implement",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 153.464,
          "end": 155.88,
          "en": "the resolve method.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 155.88,
          "end": 159.84300000000002,
          "en": "And this resolve method here now takes two arguments",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 159.84300000000002,
          "end": 163.41,
          "en": "the route, so the activated route snapshot",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 163.41,
          "end": 164.243,
          "en": "which you already know,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 164.243,
          "end": 167.46,
          "en": "which you need to import from at angular core,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 167.46,
          "end": 170.64,
          "en": "and it will also provide us the state snapshot.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 170.64,
          "end": 173.91,
          "en": "So the RouterStateSnapshot,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 173.91,
          "end": 178.14,
          "en": "which also needs to be imported from @angular/router.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 178.14,
          "end": 180.63,
          "en": "These are the two information pieces",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 180.63,
          "end": 184.02,
          "en": "the resolve method gets by angular,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 184.02,
          "end": 188.46,
          "en": "and in the end, this then also has to return",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 188.46,
          "end": 191.34,
          "en": "either an observable, which you need to import",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 191.34,
          "end": 194.07,
          "en": "from rxjs/Observable.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 194.07,
          "end": 198.3,
          "en": "This observable will then also return this type here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 198.3,
          "end": 199.53,
          "en": "So we can copy this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 199.53,
          "end": 202.17000000000002,
          "en": "but since we're creating a lot of overheads here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 202.17000000000002,
          "end": 205.53,
          "en": "we can also quickly define an interface here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 205.53,
          "end": 206.82,
          "en": "and it would of course be better",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 206.82,
          "end": 209.34,
          "en": "to outsource this in its own file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 209.34,
          "end": 211.29,
          "en": "But let's quickly do it here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 211.29,
          "end": 212.813,
          "en": "So the interface for the server",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 212.813,
          "end": 217.38,
          "en": "which has an ID of type number,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 217.38,
          "end": 219.18,
          "en": "and then the name which is a string,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 219.18,
          "end": 221.52,
          "en": "and the status, which is a string.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 221.52,
          "end": 225,
          "en": "And now this allows us to simply use server here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 225,
          "end": 227.52,
          "en": "for as a shortcut for this type.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 227.52,
          "end": 229.26,
          "en": "So the observable should in the end,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 229.26,
          "end": 231.273,
          "en": "give us back such a server,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 232.62,
          "end": 233.72,
          "en": "or we get a promise",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 233.72,
          "end": 237.54,
          "en": "which in the end will return such a server,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 237.54,
          "end": 241.65,
          "en": "or well, just such a server synchronously.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 241.65,
          "end": 244.65,
          "en": "So this is what we will get back here and resolve.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 244.65,
          "end": 248.58,
          "en": "So now we need to implement logic to get this back.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 248.58,
          "end": 253.5,
          "en": "Now we have our server's service here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 253.5,
          "end": 256.02,
          "en": "And there we have the get server method",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 256.02,
          "end": 258.51,
          "en": "which will give us back a server.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 258.51,
          "end": 260.82,
          "en": "Now this gritty is some synchronous code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 260.82,
          "end": 262.62,
          "en": "it will run instantly here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 262.62,
          "end": 265.74,
          "en": "So there is nothing wrong with this code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 265.74,
          "end": 268.98,
          "en": "we will resolve this instantly.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 268.98,
          "end": 271.59,
          "en": "And as you saw in your resolver, that's fine.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 271.59,
          "end": 275.22,
          "en": "One return possibility is to instantly return the data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 275.22,
          "end": 276.72,
          "en": "So the easiest thing we can do here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 276.72,
          "end": 279.36,
          "en": "is reach out to our server service",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 279.36,
          "end": 281.1,
          "en": "and forward as we need to inject it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 281.1,
          "end": 286.067,
          "en": "so we should provide our server serversService like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 287.28,
          "end": 288.9,
          "en": "That's a real hard word for me.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 288.9,
          "end": 291.737,
          "en": "Servers ServersService like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 294.474,
          "end": 297.27,
          "en": "And of course, if you want to inject a service",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 297.27,
          "end": 301.59,
          "en": "into another service, you have to add, @Injectable to it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 301.59,
          "end": 304.17,
          "en": "make sure to import this from at @angular/core,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 304.17,
          "end": 306.67,
          "en": "also, make sure to import your own ServersService.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 308.43,
          "end": 311.61,
          "en": "And with this, the easiest way to use this resolve function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 311.61,
          "end": 313.68,
          "en": "is to reach out to your service,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 313.68,
          "end": 315.9,
          "en": "and there we call getServer.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 315.9,
          "end": 317.25,
          "en": "And now we need to know",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 317.25,
          "end": 320.55,
          "en": "the idea of the server we have to fetch.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 320.55,
          "end": 321.75,
          "en": "Because that is what we do",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 321.75,
          "end": 324.03,
          "en": "in this server component here in the end, right?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 324.03,
          "end": 326.85,
          "en": "There in on in it, we're getting this server right now.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 326.85,
          "end": 328.5,
          "en": "So now we want to outsource this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 328.5,
          "end": 331.21,
          "en": "because let's say we want to do it before it loads.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 331.21,
          "end": 333.837,
          "en": "The good thing is, we do get the route here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 333.837,
          "end": 335.82,
          "en": "It only needs this snapshot,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 335.82,
          "end": 339.03,
          "en": "but this service here will actually run on",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 339.03,
          "end": 340.83,
          "en": "each time we re-render the route.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 340.83,
          "end": 342.346,
          "en": "So the snapshot is all we need.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 342.346,
          "end": 344.4,
          "en": "Unlike the component itself,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 344.4,
          "end": 346.89,
          "en": "again, this is executed each time.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 346.89,
          "end": 350.76,
          "en": "So no need to set up an observable or something like that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 350.76,
          "end": 353.97,
          "en": "So here we can access our route, and the route params,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 353.97,
          "end": 356.90999999999997,
          "en": "and then the id, and make sure to cast it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 356.90999999999997,
          "end": 360.33,
          "en": "with a plus sign in front of it to an integer.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 360.33,
          "end": 363.576,
          "en": "This is the easiest way of using this resolver",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 363.576,
          "end": 367.41,
          "en": "which will do the loading of our data in advance.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 367.41,
          "end": 368.88,
          "en": "And now this would also work",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 368.88,
          "end": 371.67,
          "en": "if this were to return an observable or a promise,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 371.67,
